<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Elon Musk's SpaceX aborts booster recovery due to technical issues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71afa7a105152e141945b102f3fc7178b638fa8e6d7eec2d3964b9fc25a8fc13</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:33:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues--6420a1fd1469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's SpaceX is in the midst of a 15th test-flight of its Starship rocket. The company was hoping to pull off the first-ever "double catch" - with both the booster and the ship itself coming safely back down to earth. Instead, an unspecified problem forced the company to abort recovery of the booster, which was diverted from its return path and crashed down into the Gulf of Mexico. Analysis by journalist Frédéric Castel, based in Bosa Chica, Texas, USA.</summary></entry><entry><title>Washington divided over how to deal with fallout from the Nvidia case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dab1411664948292e92c1b88cc45d3ef462e8677a54822afb5c04c0f021751c0</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case--10e578662d3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case" /><summary type="html">After the fall, the fallout. US government agencies are squabbling after AI leader Jensen Huang stepped down from chips giant Nvidia in disgrace. The Treasury says it wanted to blacklist a Singapore company at the heart of the scandal, but the Commerce Department didn't act. Megaspeed was run by suspected Chinese spy Alice Huang, who reportedly had an affair with Jensen Huang. Details by Peter O'Brien.</summary></entry><entry><title>US: What exactly caused the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd6dd72c5074e54dcd72d49df49526a29deba13252196e200d3f902e36b7d76</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years--773fa7defb8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years" /><summary type="html">After a nearly five-hour ground stoppage, flights in the US have resumed. However, officials are warning that it will take days to recover from the ongoing delays related to the incident. Transport Secretary Sean Duffy explained the crisis was due to a failure in ageing telecommunications equipment. What exactly happened? Answers with FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Transport Secretary asks Congress for $30 bn to upgrade aviation infrastructure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8eabd1df91d18e6eb890c0f21048146375f0f26e6b740ea6f7a117f088515df</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure--1fa408877d9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure" /><summary type="html">A failure in aging telecommunications equipment Friday forced a nationwide halt to departures from US airports. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says officials have found no evidence so far of a cyberattack, but that they're not ruling it out. Details by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Copper wires to blame for US flight disruption, says Trump administration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6082027bcb6dcd0089397e5ca22934f1219576716b63e512876193e3aba81e5</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:35:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration--d2146e285ca6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration" /><summary type="html">With thousands of flights cancelled and travel disruption continuing, officials say the situation should return to normal Sunday. The Trump administration pointed to aging infrastructure – specifically "a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines" – as being responsible for nationwide travel chaos.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b29ef5e77a95b0c765a8569d8c9a56b380849e14385904ce6273b6182d115049</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans--196361a3fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans" /><summary type="html">A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbcedc71330d6d98a5fc56b67fbe933eceafa66a9c2cf6ef7026a23f5cf90a08</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world--0c414d784e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3077714c2ee9815820527f38f9b9d2d22d02206df67a6fb552944f3d2d939163</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru--865ee0c1d4cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa47bd77ccbd1bc9fc58497fa52001933188f664c951e45b3bcfb767ed4e4377</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:14:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data--86cafb111fce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data" /><summary type="html">On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.</summary></entry><entry><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9e6dea8386b7891675002cb512a840fef021f5167b0c91fa417363df98c9ed</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:35:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation--ee4c7a228fe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Passengers face further disruption as US flights slowly resume after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8b6d0d74001d622f8360bd89061d07ead149543bbe09a71cca8ab2a64f48377</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T22:43:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop--a75173ff3015.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop" /><summary type="html">While flights in the United States started resuming on Saturday following the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years, more than 2,000 flights have been cancelled as airlines work to return to normal operations. Nearly 6,000 flights were cancelled on Friday, with the incident marking only the second time such an alert had been issued in US airspace since the 9/11 attacks.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a830f71f4aa8679f42b758968c34f6bcc55b2180ea14cdfb9eaa1f59023ab5e7</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:27:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issu--bea6c8926b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issue" /><summary type="html">The US flight authority on Friday halted flights across the nation due to what US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said was a communication issue affecting the country's air traffic control centres.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The Nvidia affair: Are markets about to fall out of love with AI?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e40d2bbf08da1d67fe7e7a332d1179bdfd587b096a82d26cb85d8ee18c5a6b7</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:02:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai--afdd33fb8417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang’s departure from Nvidia exposes the vulnerabilities behind the AI boom. As equities reel in response to his resignation following extramarital affairs, alleged Chinese espionage and a summons to testify before US lawmakers, questions mount over who is really in charge of tech and whether the immense capital riding on it can survive the turmoil.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitian forces recapture national stadium after two years of gang control</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3829a60ee85e967d8d1ad0c03b6e98db4006c46ac83f96aa380e8fb0ed4bc3d</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:09:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control--cac3a4adff3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces regained control Thursday, November 12, of the country's main stadium that had been under gang control for two years, forcing the national football team to play elsewhere. The Haitian National Police said in a statement that it had taken "full control" of the venue with the Task Force, a private security group serving the government, after which it left the stadium under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Devastated wasteland': Haitian security forces regain control of stadium from gangs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2727b6766103baf1ee5322ecc338cec3fabfaed0f77805e728a7f6e69d57eb4a</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:37:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-devastated-wasteland-haitian-security-forces-regain-control-of-stadium-from-gangs--b069dccdf1c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-devastated-wasteland-haitian-security-forces-regain-control-of-stadium-from-gangs" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces said they have regained control of the country's main stadium, wresting it back from the gangs that have been using it for the past two years. They were assisted by the Task Force, a private security group serving the government. The stadium is now under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers. FRANCE 24's senior reporter Catherine Norris Trent, who has covered Haiti extensively, said re-taking the stadium would be a significant step in an area of the city that had been a "devastated wasteland".</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: What does the 'blue tsunami' mean for US media?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92f2fda4eb9c7593afd927791c4475e998e98bfc6acc3090fd713f4e8c0bd19f</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:22:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261113-what-does-the-blue-tsunami-mean-for-us-media--9254bf757b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261113-what-does-the-blue-tsunami-mean-for-us-media" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at the impact of the midterm elections in the United States. While the results are being reckoned with by Republicans and celebrated by Democrats, what does it all mean for the press? Some media analysts wonder whether certain outlets, particularly ones accused of being cosy with the Trump administration, will change their tone. Our guest this week is International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>The scourge of femicide in Mexico: Impunity reigns in state of Morelos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f400c612ca6cb1d93600543cc2333a5bba953ccead6c2cc80c484764c5f306c</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:38:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261113-the-scourge-of-femicide-in-mexico-impunity-reigns-in-state-of-morelos--15b62973985d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261113-the-scourge-of-femicide-in-mexico-impunity-reigns-in-state-of-morelos" /><summary type="html">When Claudia Sheinbaum became Mexico's first female president in 2024, she pledged to tackle violence against women. And while femicides have fallen since she took office, the numbers remain alarming, with around 520 murders so far this year. In the small state of Morelos, just outside the capital Mexico City, four female students have been murdered since January, including a Spanish woman on an exchange programme. The state has one of the highest femicide rates in the country.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Peruvians flock to see Pope Leo XIV in city he served as bishop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6051c3a0b9e19b8e277dcb9dd0531f17594370e520e9bb1f72ddfa9ce0f2caa</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:55:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-peruvians-flock-to-see-pope-leo-xiv-in-city-he-served-as-bishop--3753f8041ccf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-peruvians-flock-to-see-pope-leo-xiv-in-city-he-served-as-bishop" /><summary type="html">Crowds in Peru's northern city of Chiclayo gathered early on Friday, November 13, ​ahead of ‌Pope Leo's arrival for the centerpiece event of his 12-day South America tour, an outdoor ⁠Mass with the people who called him their bishop for eight years. He declared on November 11 that the country where he served as a missionary for about 20 years was his homeland.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV meets clerical abuse victims in Peru, says Church must make 'amends'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc98d46198b391019db2abcd6bff7198728a10d778df40304b8845c380ba8a97</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-pope-leo-xiv-meets-abuse-victims-in-peru-says-church-must-make-amends--e6391118a168.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-pope-leo-xiv-meets-abuse-victims-in-peru-says-church-must-make-amends" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV met six victims of clerical abuse in Peru on Thursday, including people linked to the disbanded group Sodalitium Christianae Vitae. The US-born pontiff also urged the Catholic Church to make amends to survivors and strengthen protections against abuse as he returned to the country where he served as a missionary and bishop for nearly two decades.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitian police retake national stadium after two years of gang control</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305e9158e8b785e21feff09f1dce2b6c027395251ad4dd70aae7dba0e9af38a1</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:01:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-haitian-police-retake-national-stadium-from-gangs-after-two-years--7cf91c32db5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-haitian-police-retake-national-stadium-from-gangs-after-two-years" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces regained control of the country's main football stadium Thursday after two years under gang control, with Salvadoran troops taking over security at the venue. El Salvador deployed 2,000 soldiers to Haiti following an ambush that left four of its troops missing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Peruvian pope' Leo XIV comes home to a country that shaped his life and faith through 'hardship'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4acfb659eea50cd5228bc801bc36bb3ba295a3501f3e4b60b6dd240133346b</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T23:33:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardsh--a8e5eb904c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardship" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Casallo, Director of the Department of Philosophical and Theological Studies at Antonio Ruiz de Montoya University. Can a pope shaped by Peru's history of political violence, social inequality and religious activism help a deeply polarised nation heal and rediscover the possibility of dialogue? "We tend to see the other person not as someone who holds a different opinion, but as an enemy." Casallo argues that with Pope Leo, the first American-born pontiff's identity cannot be understood through his Chicago origins alone.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>New York building collapse kills eight, including two children</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71c627a0fab02202b08508ede2c02c8e9e178736c45d65350d201e318f0fa686</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-eight-killed-including-two-children-in-new-york-building-collapse--50be159b0c7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-eight-killed-including-two-children-in-new-york-building-collapse" /><summary type="html">Eight people, including two children, were killed when a residential building collapsed into an adjacent construction site in Brooklyn on Wednesday. Firefighters spent hours searching the rubble overnight before declaring the operation over on Thursday as authorities launched an investigation into the disaster.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>At least five people shot in DC neighbourhood near the White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bc58b1f38e136bf8d2d9e0fe058d325c10ff7372dadb422d1608a6a968a7060</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:01:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house--c1ab95e70108.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house" /><summary type="html">At least one person died after five people were shot early Thursday in a Washington, DC neighbourhood near the White House, police said. A swarm of officers responded to a nearby apartment building where a suspect was barricaded and later shot himself.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth reprimanded at war memorial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4c2b7d1de33fc3785fe69f789b3e8c57e4f93154d4771fca1d595f16c568bb2</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:51:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial--332f267ab309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial" /><summary type="html">US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, along with his wife and aides, was silenced by a guard on Wednesday at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier. Hegseth's group was at Arlington National Cemetery for a Veterans Day ceremony when they were reprimanded for laughing and taking pictures in front of the sombre memorial.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after revelations on extramarital affairs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976747da3db6afd9e2c781510e1034ba00075f30dc19dd1ca27220b93030b242</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:46:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs--11a6bfe4bbc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang resigned as chief executive of AI giant Nvidia on Thursday, November 12, after revelations he had two extramarital affairs, including one with a woman accused of spying for China. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mississippi elects its first African American to US Senate since Reconstruction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df94e8c9fc0b446054e5b20cd39c144d8fa8627c32dcc16e021098425e120182</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction--c58f82d3f782.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction" /><summary type="html">Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith to become Mississippi’s first Black US Senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory, confirmed on November 11 after prolonged ballot counting, marks a major political shift in the conservative state. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huang powers and bankrolls AI revolution: Nvidia CEO caught between 'a rock and a very hard place'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78c2246cdace62a21e5e0a54be776ee545fc9249e84929782789313d259d8235</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:11:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard---ce288d10e4d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard-place-1" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of France's Institute of Digital Sovereignty. Benhamou examines the intersection of traditional espionage, geopolitical rivalry and the extraordinary concentration of power within the global AI industry. Discussing allegations surrounding Nvidia's leadership, he describes the chipmaker as "the banker of the global AI system," a striking characterization that captures the company's importance not merely as a semiconductor manufacturer, but as a central actor in the economic and technological infrastructure underpinning the AI boom. "Because humans stay humans." Benhamou identifies one of the central paradoxes of the artificial intelligence revolution: even as technological systems acquire unprecedented strategic and economic importance, the individuals who control them remain susceptible to familiar forms of influence, manipulation and misjudgment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after affair raises national security concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f50f772504b7a1cd9d869d93a1c3331763890ff1f60967cc484730a6961051</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:06:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-affair-raises-national-security-concerns--ea3976154f31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-affair-raises-national-security-concerns" /><summary type="html">Nvidia announced on Thursday that CEO Jensen Huang was stepping down following revelations that he had an affair with a woman accused of spying for China. The company's chief financial officer Colette Kress will serve as interim CEO while the board searches for Huang's successor.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguayans get some savings back after banking collapse disrupted economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc5541b0f068c127399822b29eb58caa45dbb0c939a394e991a2994758aca566</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:24:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-paraguayans-get-some-savings-back-after-banking-collapse-disrupted-economy--3e73b54b4bc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-paraguayans-get-some-savings-back-after-banking-collapse-disrupted-economy" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's Central Bank said Wednesday, November 11, it had partially returned savings to all eligible Ueno Bank depositors locked out of their accounts when it collapsed last week. The digital bank's takeover on November 3 triggered massive protests across Paraguay and led to the impeachment and arrest of ex-president Santiago Pena, who is linked to Ueno.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scott Colom makes history in Mississippi as first Black senator in more than 140 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a044b0857a4aee36b9241de78079c70d045b8174ece77873100b249c6cdd697</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:50:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261112-scott-colom-makes-history-in-mississippi-as-first-black-senator-in-more-than-140-years--225d5e2b56d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261112-scott-colom-makes-history-in-mississippi-as-first-black-senator-in-more-than-140-years" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 12: We look at reactions from Spain after the country's first nationwide general strike in 14 years. It comes two weeks before snap general elections. Also: Scott Colom makes history as the first Black senator in Mississippi in 145 years after an epic Senate midterm race finally concluded. Finally, fans of Barça will be able to inter their ashes at Camp Nou as part of a new offer by the club to allow supporters to cheer on the team in the afterlife.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry></feed>
